# What each graph loses when it is cut up by filing. One row per graph: its independent loops
# counted across the whole corpus, and the sum of its loops counted one filing at a time.
#
# It answers an accusation rather than raising one
#   `examples/diagramming` emits one document per filing and draws the layer graph, and that is not
#   an arbitrary pick among the graphs. It is the only one whose per-filing cut keeps the graph's
#   loops, and this relation is the measurement that says so.
#
# Cutting by filing breaks the unit graph's loop
#   The unit graph's one loop runs through two filings. Across the corpus the unit graph has one
#   independent loop; summed per filing it has none, because `GPU-hour -> node-hour` and
#   `node-hour -> GPU` are filed in `every-unit-cycle`, and the edge that closes them,
#   `GPU -> GPU-hour`, is filed in `merge-holding-composition`. The fixture named
#   `every-unit-cycle` holds no loop of units on its own.
#
# The loop is the whole subject
#   `checks/conversion_cycle_does_not_close` exists to ask whether the factors close round a loop,
#   so a per-filing unit diagram would show two edges, no loop, and nothing to check: a picture that
#   is well formed, validates, and has quietly removed the one property it was drawn to show. That
#   is the failure this repository names, and making the graph a slot without measuring first would
#   produce it.
#
# Surviving the cut is not a reason to draw
#   A graph that survives is not thereby worth drawing: a graph with no edges at all, as the
#   claimants' would be, survives trivially. Survival is a precondition on an honest per-filing
#   drawing, never a reason for one.
#
# The walk lives in `rank/graph_measures.sqlc`
#   This file's `filing IS NULL` rows would be `rank/cycle_space.sqlc`'s whole output, so
#   `rank/graph_measures.sqlc` counts both scopes once, and this is the comparison between them,
#   which is the only thing here about cutting up.
-- rank/graph_measures.sqlc at both scopes: the whole against the sum of the parts.
SELECT w.graph,
       w.cycle_space_dim                                               AS corpus_wide,
       coalesce(sum(p.cycle_space_dim), 0)::bigint                     AS summed_per_filing,
       w.cycle_space_dim = coalesce(sum(p.cycle_space_dim), 0)::bigint AS survives_the_cut
FROM      (
    :compose(rank/graph_measures.sqlc)
) w
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(rank/graph_measures.sqlc)
) p ON p.graph = w.graph AND p.filing IS NOT NULL
WHERE w.filing IS NULL
GROUP BY w.graph, w.cycle_space_dim
